## Framework Adjustments to Make

Based on this evidence, here's what to change in `config/rules.yaml`:

1. __Add an OTM-only close gate for profit-taking closes.__ The framework currently lets you close at 50% profit on ANY position, even those with Δ < 0.30 and > 30 DTE remaining. Add: *"Only auto-close at 50% if |Δ| ≥ 0.30 OR DTE ≤ 21. Otherwise hold and let theta work."* This directly targets the 14 over-management losses.

2. __Raise the delta threshold for defensive closes.__ The current `csp_decision: 0.40` gate triggers too early. The GOOG/MU/MSFT/AVGO/NVDA cases all had Δ < 0.40 when closed. Change `stop_loss.delta.csp_decision` from 0.40 → __0.50__, and `cc_warn` from 0.40 → __0.50__. Only close defensively when assignment risk is REAL.

3. __Let trend-modulated profit targets do their job for CSP winners.__ The current `profit_take_csp` config already has `base_pct: 50` / `trend_target_pct: 70` / `strong_trend_target_pct: 85`. These were coded but the actual trading behavior shows closes happening at 50% regardless of trend. Make the framework __respect the trend extension__ — when the trend composite is ≥ 50 and the stock is running away from your put, don't close at 50%, hold for the 70-85% target instead.

4. __The V churn needs a brake.__ 14 V contracts in 60 days generated only +$4,487 gross (+$258 net) — lots of activity, minimal edge. The framework should flag this as over-management. Consider: *"Max 2 closes per ticker per month"* or *"No re-opening the same strike/expiry within 14 days"*.

5. __Keep the hard-stop saves as-is.__ TSLA and AMD proved the stops work. The `3x far_close`, `2x mid_close`, `1.5x near_close` premium-multiple stops are doing their job. Don't weaken them.
